    "findings": [
      {
        "result": "SOURCE_CONFIRMED_WAIT_BOUNDARIES_NOT_RUNTIME_ATTRIBUTION",
        "detail": "Client TUN reader waits for recycled buffers, then device readiness and bounded from_tun handoff. Single-carrier Tun retains up to64 reader buffers until writer encryption; bonded path snapshots into its separately bounded pool and releases Tun before queueing."
      },
      {
        "result": "SOURCE_CONFIRMED_SERVER_WAIT_BOUNDARIES",
        "detail": "Server reader waits for a shared32MiB pool, blocking device read and4096-slot handoff. Ordinary async forwarder waits for SessionMap read lock; selected stream pool/queue admission uses try_acquire/try_send rather than async capacity waits."
      },
      {
        "result": "NOT_A_PAIRED_COMPARISON",
        "detail": "All-mode matrix has legacy/one carrier; stock trace experiment has mux/two carriers. Two factors differ. Do not attribute a throughput ratio to recordizer alone or F030, pool these populations, or infer ACK timings from source waits."
      },
      {
        "result": "NO_NEW_CONFIRMED_PRODUCT_DEFECT",
        "detail": "Finite pool/queue backpressure and scheduling may explain delays, but do not establish the original asymmetry mechanism. No queue enlargement, timer priority or default change justified by this source review."
      }
